   "answer": "Based on the hyperparameter sensitivity analysis in Table 7 of the PEARL paper, the dataset-specific hyperparameter settings are as follows:\n\nFor WN18RR: batch size = 8, learning rate = 0.001, subgraph hop size k = 4, number of retained paths M = 3.\n\nFor FB15k-237: batch size = 32, learning rate = 0.0005, subgraph hop size k = 3, number of retained paths M = 3.\n\nFor NELL-995: batch size = 8, learning rate = 0.001, subgraph hop size k = 2, number of retained paths M = 5.\n\nThese values were selected according to validation performance on the V1 subsets of each dataset, as detailed in the hyperparameter sensitivity analysis section [1:60] and summarized in Table 7 [1:63]."
  },
