   "answer": "Task-CoEvolve uses the anchored deviation estimator defined as \\(\\hat{S}(h) = \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{t\\in T} \\bar{p}_t + \\frac{1}{N} \\sum_{t\\in S_k} \\frac{x_t(h) - \\bar{p}_t}{\\pi_t}\\) [3:15]. The raw outcome is not weighted directly because weighting the outcome \\(x_t(h)\\) by its inclusion probability \\(\\pi_t\\) would dominate the estimate when a task has a tiny \\(\\pi_t\\) and is consistently solved or failed, making the estimate unstable [3:15]. Instead, the deviation from the historical anchor \\(\\bar{p}_t\\) is weighted, which cancels in expectation and ensures stable comparison across iterations [3:15]."
  },
